{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"DESIGN_CONTRADICTION","classStatement":"The spec changes the approved review follow-up identity rule.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC1 (lines 52–60) requires a record per scope instance and finding ID; R1 (line 182) requires two records when an ID appears in two instances. The approved design (lines 43–48) requires one record per finding ID, with the first raising result as its origin.","failureScenario":"A finding ID appears in two ordinary review scope instances -> the spec produces two follow-ups, decisions and counts where the approved design requires one.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"API_CONTRADICTION","classStatement":"The non-review API is incompatible with the approved design.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC2 (lines 77–87) specifies recordFollowUps(core, {kind, findings}), while the approved design (lines 51–55) specifies recordFollowUps(core, {origin, findings}) with a structured dependency-scan origin.","failureScenario":"The planned dependency-scan gate calls the approved {origin, findings} API -> the specified implementation rejects or misreads the call, so the gate cannot record its follow-ups.","id":"F2","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"UNCOVERED_DESIGN_REQUIREMENT","classStatement":"The plan and rubric omit the approved measure 3 update.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"The approved design (lines 101–108) requires convergence measure 3's follow-up count to use the followUp field. AC9 and R9 (lines 157–167, 190), plan P8 and issue I-4 cover measure 2 but omit that measure 3 change.","failureScenario":"A marked run has follow-ups and convergence metrics are calculated -> implementation can pass every rubric row while measure 3 reports a count inconsistent with the new followUp rows.","id":"F3","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"RUBRIC_COVERAGE_GAP","classStatement":"R1 does not verify the stated raise-time classification inputs.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC1 (lines 55–58) requires raise-time classification using regression paths and sweep records; the failure model (lines 33–34) includes both. R1 (line 182) tests a round-4 demotion but specifies no regression-path or sweep-record case.","failureScenario":"An ordinary regression-path or sweep review raises a finding -> a classifier that ignores that path can pass R1 while omitting a required follow-up, allowing Completion without its decision.","id":"F4","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"RUBRIC_COVERAGE_GAP","classStatement":"The rubric does not verify atomic failure of bulk decisions.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC3 (lines 106–108) requires an entire multi-ID decision call to record nothing if one issue filing fails. R3 (line 184) does not test filing failure; R5 (line 186) checks only that the failed ID has no decision.","failureScenario":"A bulk new-work call files one issue and a later gh call fails -> an implementation can record decisions for earlier IDs, pass R3 and R5, yet violate the required all-or-nothing result.","id":"F5","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"RUBRIC_COVERAGE_GAP","classStatement":"R7 does not test the required contents of the generated view.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC7 (lines 149–153) requires each generated record to show severity, origin, class and failure scenario, and decided records to show decision, authority and tracking link. R7 (line 188) checks only that the file, banner and four sections exist.","failureScenario":"A follow-up view is generated with section headings but missing record details -> R7 passes although the user cannot inspect the required decision context or tracking link.","id":"F6","severity":"medium"}],"mandateAssessment":null,"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Implementation should not be authorized yet. The spec contradicts two approved design commitments, and the rubric leaves several stated behaviors unverified."}